{"uid":"b79c3ef7ddebb47a","name":"test_a_hidden_tab_issues_no_log_tail_request","fullName":"tests.test_browser_hub_backoff#test_a_hidden_tab_issues_no_log_tail_request","historyId":"4e3f9e786a68b9f7905cd03f49530b60","time":{"start":1791940405259,"stop":1791940430503,"duration":25244},"description":"Task 049 (H.7): `loadLogs` (the transcript/log-tail fetch,\n    `GET /api/runs/<id>/logs?tail=200`) is called from inside the SAME\n    `load()` that `renderRunDetail` schedules through `scheduleRefresh`\n    (see the comment above `let lastEtag = null;` in `app.js`) -- there is\n    no separate timer for it, so it already inherits both the run-detail\n    poll's back-off and its `document.hidden` pause rather than needing\n    its own wiring. This proves the pause half directly at the network\n    layer (wrapping `window.fetch` to count `/logs` calls) rather than\n    only through the timer-count instrumentation the sibling test above\n    uses, so a future change that gives the log poll its own timer without\n    routing it through the same pause point would be caught here even if\n    it left `__hubRefreshLoopCount` alone.","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task 049 (H.7): <code>loadLogs</code> (the transcript/log-tail fetch,<br />\n<code>GET /api/runs/&lt;id&gt;/logs?tail=200</code>) is called from inside the SAME<br />\n<code>load()</code> that <code>renderRunDetail</code> schedules through <code>scheduleRefresh</code><br />\n(see the comment above <code>let lastEtag = null;</code> in <code>app.js</code>) -- there is<br />\nno separate timer for it, so it already inherits both the run-detail<br />\npoll's back-off and its <code>document.hidden</code> pause rather than needing<br />\nits own wiring. This proves the pause half directly at the network<br />\nlayer (wrapping <code>window.fetch</code> to count <code>/logs</code> calls) rather than<br />\nonly through the timer-count instrumentation the sibling test above<br />\nuses, so a future change that gives the log poll its own timer without<br />\nrouting it through the same pause point would be caught here even if<br />\nit left <code>__hubRefreshLoopCount</code> alone.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791939562063,"stop":1791939562063,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791939562063,"stop":1791939562063,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791940405254,"stop":1791940405254,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_task_record_dir","time":{"start":1791940405255,"stop":1791940405256,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791940405255,"stop":1791940405255,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_scrub_notifier_env_in_process","time":{"start":1791940405256,"stop":1791940405257,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_stub_escalation_backoff_at_class_level","time":{"start":1791940405257,"sto